httpx2 is a fully featured HTTP client for Python, with sync and async
APIs. It is the maintained successor of httpx, installable alongside it.

It installs the upstream pure-Python wheel: the sdist cannot be built
without uv-dynamic-versioning, which is not packaged.

The httpx2 command line tool needs the optional click, python3-rich and
python3-pygments packages. The library itself does not.

Requires Python 3.10 or newer, so it does not build on Slackware 15.0.
